module compiled ahead: key its source's (AotKey; \"\" for the main module,"] [51 1 "// which AotMain runs from its text), ir its IR text, natives its code objects' functions in pre-order."] [59 1 "// aotAttach is ReadIR's hook: the native functions of a registered IR text set on its code objects."] [86 1 "// aotCompile is a compiled program's compiler (SetCompiler): a source compiled ahead, else the host's."] [102 1 "// hostCompile asks the host's compiler (the command PYI_AOT_COMPILER names, started once: arbace.python.aot"] [103 1 "// compile-server) for source's IR: a request \"MODE\\tFILE\\tBYTES\\n\" and the source, an answer \"BYTES\\n\""] [104 1 "// and the compiler's text (arbace.python.run/compile-source's: the IR, SyntaxError: ..., incomplete)."] [155 1 "// AotMain is a compiled program's process: sys.argv and sys.path as bin/pyi run gives them, the"] [156 1 "// compiler of source at run time, the main module's IR run as __main__ (RunModule); the exit status."] [157 1 "// PYI_AOT_STATS names a file for the code objects run compiled and on the loop, and the host's compiles."] [179 1 "// AotBadPC is a compiled function entered at a PC that is not an instruction's."] [184 1 "// The helpers of the compiled code: each is an operation of step's switch (eval.go) with its argument"] [185 1 "// a constant; the ones that may raise return the error, a call also a *pushFrame."] [372 1 "// AotToBool is to-bool (not false) and not (not true)."] [509 1 "// AotForIter is for-iter: the next item pushed (false), or at the end the iterator popped (true)."] [514 22 "// FOR_ITER clears a raised StopIteration: the loop's end"] [527 1 "// AotTruthy is the popped value's truth (the conditional jumps')."] [561 1 "// AotCall is call [N KWNAMES] (kw the kwnames tuple's constant index, or -1): a Python function's"] [562 1 "// frame pushed (the *pushFrame returned: f.PC must be the next instruction's), a generator made, or"] [563 1 "// any other callable called."] [623 1 "// AotExec runs instruction i of f's code as step runs it, for the operations the compiled code does not"] [624 1 "// spell out: the rarer ones of step's switch and every operation another file registers (RegisterOp)."] [625 1 "// f.PC is the next instruction's when it is called; an operation that jumps sets it."] [757 1 "// AotPopIsNone pops the top and tells whether it is None (jump-if-none, jump-if-not-none)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[70 32] [88 47] [116 42] [118 40] [132 86] [147 41] [161 37] [162 28] [172 36] [263 41] [276 36] [296 57] [416 12] [416 28] [417 40] [429 22] [494 25] [494 33] [513 28] [578 47] [583 35] [634 29] [642 62] [647 24] [650 62] [657 44] [664 29] [674 17] [674 31] [678 22] [678 30] [689 37] [708 30]]} (go/file "aot.go" :imports [


